## bugreports

- [x] settings.py: `Settings.load_configuration()` reads hardware config from `Path(__file__).parent / "hardware_config.yaml"` (alarmclock/core/hardware_config.yaml), but that file doesn't exist there — the real one lives at config/hardware_config.yaml (daemon.py already points there correctly). Currently raises FileNotFoundError whenever load_configuration() is called.
      -> moot: load_configuration() and hardware_config.yaml/.py are both gone, see CONFIG_REFACTOR_PLAN.md

- [ ] KeyboardInterrupt handling in daemon.py: When Ctrl+C is pressed during execution, the program may crash instead of shutting down gracefully. The try/except block around the main loop should catch KeyboardInterrupt but may not be working properly due to how asyncio.run() handles exceptions during initialization vs execution.

- [ ] fix logger showing itself as the calling module, even if the daemon called it
      (separate from the module_name/*args ordering bug fixed in this refactor - that one made
      positional format args silently swallowed, e.g. "webui listening on %s:%s"; this one is
      about the displayed module name itself when none is passed)
- [x] fix settings and hardware_config.py loading (config refactor, see CONFIG_REFACTOR_PLAN.md)

